{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms","id":267838,"title":"Will Lunar forms limit Lunar Charms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-28T19:18:44-07:00","id":267838,"title":"Will Lunar forms limit Lunar Charms?","content":"Can a Lunar use an Appearance Charm to appear heartwarmingly adorable... as an emaciated lion with fresh blood dripping from its fangs?<br /> <br /> Can a Lunar use a Manipulation Charm to appear mind-shatteringly scary... as a cute little bunny rabbit?<br /> <br /> Can a Lunar use a version of Graceful Crane Stance to balance on a tree leaf... as Mount Mostah?<br /> <br /> <br /> Just how much are the strengths and weaknesses of a Lunar's current form going to impact the effect of their Charms?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T19:33:42-07:00","id":267866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms#post267838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Lunar use an Appearance Charm to appear heartwarmingly adorable... as an emaciated lion with fresh blood dripping from its fangs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Though I think the ST would have a right to impose a penalty to the roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms#post267838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Lunar use a Manipulation Charm to appear mind-shatteringly scary... as a cute little bunny rabbit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Though I think the ST would have a right to impose a penalty to the roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms#post267838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Lunar use a version of Graceful Crane Stance to balance on a tree leaf... as Mount Mostah?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though the likelihood of a given Lunar having Mount Mostath's heart's blood is pretty slim. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms#post267838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just how much are the strengths and weaknesses of a Lunar's current form going to impact the effect of their Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't affect it at all in 2e. I anticipate the effect will be the same in 3e, because making Charms be form-dependent adds nothing to the game but takes a lot away from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T19:53:57-07:00","id":267884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms#post267838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Lunar use an Appearance Charm to appear heartwarmingly adorable... as an emaciated lion with fresh blood dripping from its fangs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can a Lunar use a Manipulation Charm to appear mind-shatteringly scary... as a cute little bunny rabbit?[/quote]<br /> There's general social penalties for doing stuff like trying to make repartee at a fancy gala while covered in blood. I imagine the same would apply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can a Lunar use a version of Graceful Crane Stance to balance on a tree leaf... as Mount Mostah? </div> </div> </div>Assuming a wording as absolute as 2e, then yes. Can't say whether they'll have an equivalent effect in Ex3 one way or the other.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just how much are the strengths and weaknesses of a Lunar's current form going to impact the effect of their Charms? </div> </div> </div>Some forms are synergistic with certain charms (being a tyrant lizard + grappling charms = get fucking wrecked). Some forms may be antisynergistic (be a fish + grappling charms = what the fuck am I gonna do with these fins). <br /> <br /> Will Lunar Charms have built-in synergies with certain forms? It could happen! Will they have built in anti-synergies? Probably not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T20:19:44-07:00","id":267899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=267866#post267866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They didn't affect it at all in 2e. I anticipate the effect will be the same in 3e, because making Charms be form-dependent adds nothing to the game but takes a lot away from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would disagree. If it's carelessly slapped on, yes, it would probably be a bad idea. If it's done as part of their core design to encourage a particular and fun play style, though, it could add quite a bit. At least for the strengths side of the equation, we know it was certainly something they'd considered for a while, in the form of the Protean keyword.<br /> <br /> It remains a pity the old forums went kaput, as I don't know if anyone saved it, but for a while it was to be a component of 2e's Lunarrata. If I remember correctly, a Charm with that keyword could be used normally for a standard benefit, but would also enable a Lunar to perform a reflexive and instantaneous shapeshifting action into a resonant form for that Charm, with a non-trivial benefit toward the action it enhanced (limiting the benefit of the activation to once per creature shape per scene). The example was of a Charm meant to enhance a piercing, charging attack, with examples of resonant forms including creatures known for such charging forms of attack, such as a bull, a ram, a boar, or a narwhal. Holden later said the keyword ultimately got the kibosh, but only at the time he said they'd decided on a better implementation. It all sounded very cool, seeing shapechanging into appropriate forms rewarded.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if they're considering or considered some sort of penalty or outright disability for particularly... unresonant (irresonant? eh, whateva) forms for particular Charms, and admit it's harder to see a way of that enhancing the fun. Possibly &quot;this is an effect we really want Lunars to have, but forms like X would be obvious ways to make it so totally broken we couldn't in good conscience let it through, so they're off-limits for it,&quot; I don't know. I personally would rather they go for an all-carrot approach than wedging a stick in this area. Having the form a Lunar assumes play a role in the effectiveness some (likely not all) of their Charms possess can give a distinctive quality to their play style options. I doubt it'll be the only one, but I see something like it as a strong candidate for inclusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T20:19:53-07:00","id":267900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=267884#post267884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assuming a wording as absolute as 2e, then yes. Can't say whether they'll have an equivalent effect in Ex3 one way or the other.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>2e wasn't so absolute, as it had a half-ton weight limit, which Mount Mostath clearly exceeds by a vast margin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T20:41:57-07:00","id":267933,"title":"","content":"a kitty with strength charms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T20:42:04-07:00","id":267934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=267884#post267884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some forms may be antisynergistic (be a fish + grappling charms = what the fuck am I gonna do with these fins).</div> </div> </div> </div>Bite attack!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T20:53:57-07:00","id":267947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=267899#post267899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's done as part of their core design to encourage a particular and fun play style, though, it could add quite a bit. At least for the strengths side of the equation, we know it was certainly something they'd considered for a while, in the form of the Protean keyword.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more from the perspective of &quot;unless you're in Form X, you can't use this Charm&quot; versus &quot;you get bennies to this Charm if you're in Form X.&quot; The latter is cool and plays up form thematics; the former is restrictive in a way I don't like. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=267899#post267899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly &quot;this is an effect we really want Lunars to have, but forms like X would be obvious ways to make it so totally broken we couldn't in good conscience let it through, so they're off-limits for it,&quot; I don't know. I personally would rather they go for an all-carrot approach than wedging a stick in this area. Having the form a Lunar assumes play a role in the effectiveness some (likely not all) of their Charms possess can give a distinctive quality to their play style options. I doubt it'll be the only one, but I see something like it as a strong candidate for inclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they should flat-out rethink that effect if it's broken in cool forms? Makes me think a bit about what we've seen with DBT/Evocations, the trading-off of power. There I think it's kind of appropriate, but I have some problems with the notion that your shapeshifting (an inherent thing you can do as a Lunar Exalt) and your Charms (the expression of internal excellence you possess as a Lunar Exalt) would ever be truly incompatible, just in some cases less-than-optimally paired together (e.g. trying to look super pretty and pleasant when you're in a vicious-looking gaunt barghast form).<br /> <br /> I do prefer the all-carrot method too. To me it's better to tell players &quot;well, you CAN do X with Y but you'll take a penalty&quot; than it is to say &quot;you absolutely cannot do X with Y, not because of balance but because we don't like it.&quot; The former allows people to stick in their comfort zone if they choose to be a super demure claw strider; the latter basically says &quot;you're Doing It Wrong&quot; and honestly I have had more than enough of authors tell me I'm Doing It Wrong in the last 2 eds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T21:03:30-07:00","id":267957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=267899#post267899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly &quot;this is an effect we really want Lunars to have, but forms like X would be obvious ways to make it so totally broken we couldn't in good conscience let it through, so they're off-limits for it,&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer to design around that if at all possible. &quot;No, you can't use your best combat Charms while you're an ox-dragon, that would be <i>too good</i>&quot; is a pretty lame thing to hear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T21:17:56-07:00","id":267961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=267957#post267957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd prefer to design around that if at all possible. &quot;No, you can't use your best combat Charms while you're an ox-dragon, that would be <i>too good</i>&quot; is a pretty lame thing to hear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no question. My meaning -- in that off-the-cuff and not-long-considered idea -- was more to the tune of &quot;no, you can't use this Charm while you're a creature that has this rather particular property, because the interaction of those two just goes straight to Crazy Town.&quot; Which... having posted, I realize is not far removed from what you said. Eh, beside the point: it still wouldn't be a good thing to say, and designing around such things would certainly be preferred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Minor editin'. 09-29-2014, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T21:37:50-07:00","id":267968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=267947#post267947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking more from the perspective of &quot;unless you're in Form X, you can't use this Charm&quot; versus &quot;you get bennies to this Charm if you're in Form X.&quot; The latter is cool and plays up form thematics; the former is restrictive in a way I don't like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but I have to ask you, what about Charms that you can use in a lot of Forms, but not in all of them? Or one that you CAN use in a lot of forms, but it's not always useful. I'll use Vance's example, like using Grappling charms when your Form is a tuna.<br /> <br /> On a sidenote, how good would a Snake-form be at Grappling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T21:48:25-07:00","id":267971,"title":"","content":"I will just step in and say that if I can't do my patented one-inch-lemur-punch, I'll be disappointed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T21:50:32-07:00","id":267972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=267968#post267968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, but I have to ask you, what about Charms that you can use in a lot of Forms, but not in all of them? Or one that you CAN use in a lot of forms, but it's not always useful. I'll use Vance's example, like using Grappling charms when your Form is a tuna.<br /> <br /> On a sidenote, how good would a Snake-form be at Grappling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Regular size snake? Not great.<br /> <br /> Big ass constrictor? Hella.<br /> <br /> Titanoboa? <i>Hella</i> hella.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T21:58:01-07:00","id":267974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=267968#post267968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, but I have to ask you, what about Charms that you can use in a lot of Forms, but not in all of them? Or one that you CAN use in a lot of forms, but it's not always useful. I'll use Vance's example, like using Grappling charms when your Form is a tuna.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would probably make things feel more natural if particular and obvious non-Charm actions can certainly be cut off or heavily penalized by one's shape. Passing on a message in a hand-based sign language is just not gonna work for the majority of animals. It doesn't matter how many Charms you have that would enhance such a means of passing on a message: you can't enhance an action you can't take. Though I imagine stunting and Charms may let a Lunar get around some such constraints. Something like Dog Tongue Method will probably still exist for Lunars to talk while animals, say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On a sidenote, how good would a Snake-form be at Grappling? </div> </div> </div>Probably depends on the type of snake and how robust grappling is. If options are plentiful, lacking limbs may cut off some of them as a matter of course. If it's a big snake that's known for coiling around and strangling its victims, options that can use that would probably be scary. There may also be perks for the unusual body shape your opponent must now try to grapple against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T22:59:56-07:00","id":268028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=267961#post267961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, no question. My meaning -- in that off-the-cuff and not-long-considered idea -- was more to the tune of &quot;no, you can't use this Charm while you're a creature that has this rather particular property, because the interaction of those two just goes straight to Crazy Town.&quot; Which... having posted, I realize is not far removed from what you said. Eh, beside the point: it still wouldn't be a good thing to say, and designing around such things would certainly be preferred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a better way to word it would be using charms in a form with unintended consequences. Like, say, an attack that gave one extra damage for every two limbs, so two for most humans and like four for an octopus/spider or five for a squid...forgetting for a moment that the Fanged Wentibla of the Two Hundred Arms is a creature in the corebook.<br /> <br /> Then again that kind of thing should probably be easy to catch, I hope, because I need to transform into a yeddim before I bullrush a raksha through a wall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T05:53:27-07:00","id":268192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms#post267838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Lunar use an Appearance Charm to appear heartwarmingly adorable... as an emaciated lion with fresh blood dripping from its fangs?<br /> <br /> Can a Lunar use a Manipulation Charm to appear mind-shatteringly scary... as a cute little bunny rabbit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think that if the shapeshifters are using Charms to look like a certain thing, that would entail... looking like that thing.<br /> <br /> If you're in the shape of an emaciated lion and use a Charm to appear adorable, you'll subtly shift emphasis until you look like an adorable lion. Hell, even the emaciation might actually help, if it changes emphasis to look less dangerous and more sympathetic.<br /> <br /> That's what I would think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T06:27:17-07:00","id":268213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=268192#post268192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that if the shapeshifters are using Charms to look like a certain thing, that would entail... looking like that thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, pretty much.<br /> <br /> The OP question is predicated on the assumption that your form can only look like one specific thing with one specific mien. I don't have any reason to think that assumption is correct - if <a href=\"http://33.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m8q57y5ohv1rdik7po1_500.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">cutethulhu</a> has taught me anything, it's that the presentation of a creature is much more important than its shape in terms of how people receive it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T07:10:18-07:00","id":268228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=267900#post267900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e wasn't so absolute, as it had a half-ton weight limit, which Mount Mostath clearly exceeds by a vast margin.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;He treats it as a three-footwide ledge capable of supporting a thousand pounds of weight when determining what movement and Athletics actions he can take and what penalties to them might apply.&quot;<br /> <br /> I always forget this clause, because the wording seems to place restrictions on the leaf rather than the Exalt, and I don't care about the leaf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T07:30:47-07:00","id":268254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=268228#post268228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;He treats it as a three-footwide ledge capable of supporting a thousand pounds of weight when determining what movement and Athletics actions he can take and what penalties to them might apply.&quot;<br /> <br /> I always forget this clause, because the wording seems to place restrictions on the leaf rather than the Exalt, and I don't care about the leaf.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was always on my mind as one of the few potential balance points where one might choose a tiger or claw strider over a tyrant lizard. Want to be a <i>T. rex</i>? Alright, but you won't be doing wuxia leaps onto slender willow branches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T07:32:50-07:00","id":268256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=267968#post267968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or one that you CAN use in a lot of forms, but it's not always useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more fine with this.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of the example of one of your forms being an emaciated lion that just looks crazed because when you took it's Heart's Blood, it was half-starved and going mad from hunger. If this is the form that a group of locals finds you in, you don't necessarily want to be forced to shift into a cute lil bunny form in order to do some kinds of social-fu - maybe you're trying to get them to care for the local lions, maybe you don't want to reveal yourself as an Exalt (and shapeshifting would, at the very least, reveal you as not a normal thing). So they find you in this form and you unleash some non-verbal Charms, which you're using to...I dunno, create an Intimacy tied to emaciated lions and evoke feelings of pity and protectiveness of them. Since this isn't a cute and cuddly form, maybe they get a bonus to resist or you take a penalty. Either way you still get to try and accomplish your goal in the form you choose to be in, without being forced to change forms to accomplish that goal with your Charms<br /> <br /> And you should be able to use these same Charms in yeddim shape to maybe warm the hearts of caravan-drivers who beat yeddim, or in stag shape to awe hunters into no longer hunting trophy bucks, or in salmon shape to convince them not to overfish, or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T08:43:40-07:00","id":268279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=267972#post267972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regular size snake? Not great.<br /> <br /> Big ass constrictor? Hella.<br /> <br /> Titanoboa? <i>Hella</i> hella.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would disagree with this slightly.<br /> <br /> Depends on what you are grappling, if you're talking about grappling something human sized all is right, however if it's the epic battle between a Lunar and a Mouse of the Sun, that Regular sized snake is going to be a lot better at it than a Titanoboa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T09:41:35-07:00","id":268304,"title":"","content":"I wonder, if you're sufficiently large, can stepping or sitting or otherwise placing most of your mass atop an opponent qualify as a grapple?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T10:52:39-07:00","id":268346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=268279#post268279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would disagree with this slightly.<br /> <br /> Depends on what you are grappling, if you're talking about grappling something human sized all is right, however if it's the epic battle between a Lunar and a Mouse of the Sun, that Regular sized snake is going to be a lot better at it than a Titanoboa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woof woof woof woof :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T10:55:44-07:00","id":268349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=268304#post268304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder, if you're sufficiently large, can stepping or sitting or otherwise placing most of your mass atop an opponent qualify as a grapple?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say sure - that's basically a ready-made stunt for crushing damage.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm really hoping for something like the protean keyword to encourage shapeshifting in combat. I'm also hoping - one way or another - that they won't penalise players to hell and back for wanting to shapeshift in combat.<br /> <br /> Form Lock, I'm talking about you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T11:00:33-07:00","id":268352,"title":"","content":"I want details about how Vance is personally going to slowly torture formlock to death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T11:47:34-07:00","id":268413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=267884#post267884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some forms are synergistic with certain charms (being a tyrant lizard + grappling charms = get fucking wrecked).</div> </div> </div> </div>Truly, the mightiest grappling arms in Creation are these:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://cdn.instructables.com/FY7/OOKS/HLJUZSS2/FY7OOKSHLJUZSS2.LARGE.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T11:51:56-07:00","id":268418,"title":"","content":"Does biting count as a grapple?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T11:55:39-07:00","id":268419,"title":"","content":"I don't know, but it's funnier to imagine Tyrant Lizards having to do it with those stubby little arms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T11:56:50-07:00","id":268422,"title":"","content":"If it makes sense as a grapple, it can be a grapple. Tyrant lizard clamps down on you and picks you up into the air? That's a grapple. Kitten tries to do the same thing? Not so much. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:white\">unless you're a mouse whatEVER</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T11:59:17-07:00","id":268424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=268422#post268422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it makes sense as a grapple, it can be a grapple. Tyrant lizard clamps down on you and picks you up into the air? That's a grapple. Kitten tries to do the same thing? Not so much.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:white\">unless you're a mouse whatEVER</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What if its trying to grapple your (metaphorical)heart?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T12:12:33-07:00","id":268437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=268419#post268419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, but it's funnier to imagine Tyrant Lizards having to do it with those stubby little arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each of which is surmised by CAD engineering programs to have had a pull capacity of 400 lbs or more, not counting the power from nearby muscles.. Not much motion distance on them, but don't try to wrestle with the &quot;tiny arms&quot; for fun, because you'll get mangled for your trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T12:51:00-07:00","id":268475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms#post267838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Lunar use a Manipulation Charm to appear mind-shatteringly scary... as a cute little bunny rabbit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why bother using a charm when extreme violence would be just as effective?<br /> <img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/13/137152/3832384-8592826236-holy-.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T12:57:11-07:00","id":268477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=268413#post268413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Truly, the mightiest grappling arms in Creation are these:</div> </div> </div> </div>Who needs ARMS when you can just grab them in your jaws and thrash violently?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T18:28:59-07:00","id":268652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=268475#post268475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caerbannog</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that's a valid stunt for Social Combat. After all, what are Extras for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T22:48:03-07:00","id":268809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=268475#post268475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why bother using a charm when extreme violence would be just as effective?<br /> <img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/13/137152/3832384-8592826236-holy-.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Because the example was a <i>Manipulation</i>-based Charm, not Charisma. Manipulation based intimidation is for <i>bluffing</i>, because you don't actually have the strength or motivation to rip someone apart.<br /> <br /> In this case, it would be a newbie Lunar hiding his human face from a mob by using his Spirit Shape, and using one of his few Charms to trick them into thinking that he's terribly dangerous despite being only a cute little bunny with nothing but social magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T03:50:34-07:00","id":268924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=268419#post268419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, but it's funnier to imagine Tyrant Lizards having to do it with those stubby little arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those stubby arms are strong, so they will bite you then use them like meat hooks so you can not run away....<br /> <br /> If you want real stubby useless arms look at the carnotaurus<br /> <img src=\"http://blogs.smithsonianmag.com/dinosaur/files/2010/12/abelisaurid-arms.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://palaeos.com/vertebrates/theropoda/images/Carnotaurus.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","user":"MuscaDomestica","date":". 09-30-2014, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","name":"MuscaDomestica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T08:31:44-07:00","id":269114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=268809#post268809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this case, it would be a newbie Lunar hiding his human face from a mob by using his Spirit Shape, and using one of his few Charms to trick them into thinking that he's terribly dangerous despite being only a cute little bunny with nothing but social magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I was thinking of regarding the examples is that what is cute and what is scary tends to be fairly subjective to people, especially when it comes to animals. I mean, there are people in real life who won't stand to have a rabbit anywhere near them, because they find them terrifying. Even I, if I stretch my imagination a bit, can see some of their features in terms that seem more creepy than cute (especially around the eyes, and the curve of the clawed toes on their hind legs).<br /> <br /> If part of Lunars is that they shape perceptions of themselves, I'd find it fairly suitable to have Appearance Charms that help take some of that subjectivity away; that everybody who looks at you experiences you in the terms that somebody with a phobia of rabbits would (or whatever other context has somebody not looking on them favourably).<br /> <br /> Maybe also something where you seem to dreadfully portend something; they don't see a rabbit, they see evidence that a swarm that will destroy their crops is about to arrive, or even already here, and rush away to build fences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T09:51:54-07:00","id":269210,"title":"","content":"Have you ever seen a rabbit stretch?<br /> <br /> It's like something out of the War of the Worlds. Each leg is longer than their body.<br /> <br /> It looks plain unnatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T10:05:12-07:00","id":269225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=269210#post269210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever seen a rabbit stretch?<br /> <br /> It's like something out of the War of the Worlds. Each leg is longer than their body.<br /> <br /> It looks plain unnatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, like most of the character designs from XXXHOLiC then? (^VVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T10:09:01-07:00","id":269229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=269114#post269114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If part of Lunars is that they shape perceptions of themselves, I'd find it fairly suitable to have Appearance Charms that help take some of that subjectivity away; that everybody who looks at you experiences you in the terms that somebody with a phobia of rabbits would (or whatever other context has somebody not looking on them favourably).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of a (non-Exalted) character I have who was reshaped by a faerie, who was herself defined by beauty. As a consequence, it's just not possible for him to appear less than aesthetically pleasing to all eyes and senses -- though it varies whether he's deemed physically attractive, cute (in the manner of a child or pet), just nice to look at (in the manner of a lovely scenery or piece of art), or any other spin. I could certainly see similar principles in play for this and other Lunar powers.<br /> <br /> While I like that notion of being able to achieve a minimum level of terror/beauty/whathaveyou, I'm also fond of the notion that picking the right shape for the job should be rewarding. I'd like to see such a power make a rabbit seem frightening even to those who normally wouldn't think so, in addition to making that rabbit seem <i>especially</i> frightening to those who already rightly fear the lagomorph menace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T10:43:33-07:00","id":269256,"title":"","content":"Have you ever watched a rabbit <i>yawn?</i> It's pretty horrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T13:53:19-07:00","id":269451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hushnowquietnow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=269256#post269256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever watched a rabbit <i>yawn?</i> It's pretty horrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's let the fine members of the OPP Exalted forums be the judges of that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GqrPy-Y-UKw\" data-code=\"GqrPy-Y-UKw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/GqrPy-Y-UKw/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T21:49:05-07:00","id":269832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=267884#post267884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some forms may be antisynergistic (be a fish + grappling charms = what the fuck am I gonna do with these fins).</div> </div> </div> </div>But just think how devastating it must feel like to be grappled by a fish.<br /> *Then as I was pile-drivered into the ground by the salmon, I began to wonder at what point my life had begun to go so wrong...*<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T23:44:06-07:00","id":269886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=269832#post269832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But just think how devastating it must feel like to be grappled by a fish.<br /> *Then as I was pile-drivered into the ground by the salmon, I began to wonder at what point my life had begun to go so wrong...*</div> </div> </div> </div>Long have I been delighted with the thought of a Lunar who successfully embarrasses others by kicking the ever-loving crap out of them as a mouse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T16:46:45-07:00","id":271192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=269886#post269886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Long have I been delighted with the thought of a Lunar who successfully embarrasses others by kicking the ever-loving crap out of them as a mouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really, really want to make a martial arts master who's preferred form is that of a preying mantis. So worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T17:54:49-07:00","id":271257,"title":"","content":"Only thing I can think of that a Lunar's form is going to Limit is Evocations. I beleive one of the Dev's said that Lunar's can't use Evocations while in Deadly Beastman Form, but that is about the only Lunar form related &quot;charm&quot; limitations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank"