ank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T10:33:29-07:00","id":272335,"title":"","content":"Yeah. That does seem like a total lunar thing to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T11:19:18-07:00","id":272380,"title":"","content":"&quot;They see me growling<br /> They hating<br /> Wyld Hunting and trying to catch me Shapeshifting.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T11:21:44-07:00","id":272385,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Chicken Boo would be a viable concept for a Lunar...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T17:34:51-07:00","id":272592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hushnowquietnow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=269256#post269256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever watched a rabbit <i>yawn?</i> It's pretty horrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>My cousin had a cute little tiny bunny that would give me flashbacks to this scene whenever I got my fingers near his cage to feed him:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/zqzHdKqZAmo?t=1m48s\" data-code=\"zqzHdKqZAmo\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/zqzHdKqZAmo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T00:13:28-07:00","id":272789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=268809#post268809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the example was a <i>Manipulation</i>-based Charm, not Charisma. Manipulation based intimidation is for <i>bluffing</i>, because you don't actually have the strength or motivation to rip someone apart.</div> </div> </div> </div> What kind of namby pamby lagomorphs have you run into?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://dauntlessmedia.net/wp-content/gallery/watership-down/watership-down-00289.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T08:14:58-07:00","id":272945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=272789#post272789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What kind of namby pamby lagomorphs have you run into?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://dauntlessmedia.net/wp-content/gallery/watership-down/watership-down-00289.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Why are you running? Dogs aren't dangerous!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T09:18:47-07:00","id":272967,"title":"","content":"Rabbits are kind of weird on that; they've got the teeth, claws and generally aggressive and territorial attitude, but they can also make for fairly passive prey animals, even occasionally dying of heart attacks when faced with predators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T09:29:46-07:00","id":272970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=272789#post272789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What kind of namby pamby lagomorphs have you run into?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about rabbits.<br /> <br /> The &quot;you&quot; is the Lunar faced with an entire Wyld Hunt, with no backup. <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://dauntlessmedia.net/wp-content/gallery/watership-down/watership-down-00289.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>[/QUOTE]<br /> Fucking movie.<br /> <br /> Just because it's animated and about bunny rabbits doesn't mean it's okay for four year old boys to watch! READ THE RATINGS!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T09:57:25-07:00","id":273010,"title":"","content":"I have another question that isn't about killer rabbits and movie-related childhood trauma's.<br /> <br /> Recently, during a game of Dota, I realized that the character of Broodmother (basically, giant spider, can conjure up babby-spiders, monstrous in one-on-one combat.) Would be a very decent Lunar character.<br /> Now, her abilties are very spider-y, she spins webs, spawns swarms of spiderlings at a time and drinks her enemies vital fluids to restore her own health. Would these abilities by limited to just her spider-form, or can she use these in her human form as well? Would these sorts of very specific abilities be Essence 5+ material? Your input is appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T12:12:39-07:00","id":273138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=272970#post272970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about rabbits.<br /> <br /> The &quot;you&quot; is the Lunar faced with an entire Wyld Hunt, with no backup.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say intimidating an entire wyld hunt as a rabbit would be a bit silly, but doable. Generally I'd say it'd be more practical to use forms like that to flee or hide yourself somewhere they cannot reach and save the intimidation for more conventionally intimidating creatures. Or using a war form. Or turning yourself into some bizarre chimeric monstrosity that happens to feature rabbit ears and teeth, maybe claws.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T12:22:28-07:00","id":273141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/267838-will-lunar-forms-limit-lunar-charms?p=273010#post273010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have another question that isn't about killer rabbits and movie-related childhood trauma's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, but isn't everything <i>really</i> about that, when you drill down far enough, possibly in imaginary directions? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Recently, during a game of Dota, I realized that the character of Broodmother (basically, giant spider, can conjure up babby-spiders, monstrous in one-on-one combat.) Would be a very decent Lunar character.<br /> Now, her abilties are very spider-y, she spins webs, spawns swarms of spiderlings at a time and drinks her enemies vital fluids to restore her own health. Would these abilities by limited to just her spider-form, or can she use these in her human form as well? </div> </div> </div>I could see a case for either. I'm certainly in favor of most such abilities being <i>more effective</i> in her monstrous spider-form, regardless of whether her human form can pull them off. I'm at this point guessing, if they appear nowhere else, that somewhat personalized Charm trees may be able to build off of DBT or the like, for particular use in that form.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would these sorts of very specific abilities be Essence 5+ material? Your input is appreciated. </div> </div> </div>I think I know what you're referring to with the mention of Essence 5+, and I really don't think that's what the devs meant by it. Unless it's just the sort of power they want in the game for an Exalt and also don't want to be accessible to normal PCs (they mentioned Leviathan's whale-zilla bit as all they could think up) or that it represents a personal mastery in a somewhat specific way that's perhaps beyond what the splat is really about (which, per Holden's example involving a young Lunar learning an elder Lunar's technique that I still really really really wish hadn't been lost on the old forums, would also be something a non-E5+ character <i>could</i> learn at a lower Essence rating, even if it's not as simple as &quot;pay xp, get Charm), I don't think it's meant to fall in the E5+ range. Admittedly, we also kind of don't know a lot about that, so I'm not sure how much good speculation does at this point. &gt;.&gt; I should also probably try to sound less authoritative on the topic, but it's the sense I got from it.<br /> <br /> In any case, those sorts of powers feel like the sorts of things that Lunars -- being meant to draw off monsters and beasts -- should have solidly in their wheelhouse. I would find it very confusing, surprising, and disappointing if Lunars couldn't break out supernatural powers resonant with their totems until their Essence went beyond the assumed E1-5 play experience. That would seem directly counter to what the devs are trying to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}